cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the merged dataset it builds, please cite the software archive below, and cite the accompanying paper for the analysis itself."
type: software
title: "dem-crime-equity: analysis code for estimating racial disparity in imprisonment when the measures disagree"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a state-year study of racial disparity in imprisonment across the United States.
  The repository rebuilds the merged panel from public sources (the State Democracy Index 2.0, the
  Vera Institute's Incarceration Trends, and University of Florida Election Lab turnout), and
  reproduces every model and figure in the accompanying paper: cross-sectional comparisons under
  four competing disparity measures, within and between state (Mundlak) mixed models, group-based
  multivariate trajectory models, a synthetic control for Florida's 2018 felon re-enfranchisement,
  a sixteen-specification curve, and a joint Bayesian multilevel model of the log Black and log
  white imprisonment rates with first-order autoregressive errors, from which each competing
  disparity measure is read off as a contrast of a single posterior. Robustness scripts cover a
  negative-binomial count model, census-region fixed effects, a Hispanic recording-practice screen,
  a national decomposition of the trend, and the same measurement reversal on poverty,
  urbanization, and the party of the governor.
